				7
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Eliminate local `::Vine::Client` and `::Cache` re-exports\n\nReplace the final deviating local import patterns (`use ::Vine::Client as Client` and `use ::Cache::X as X`) with direct absolute-path imports (`use ::Vine::Client` and `use ::Cache::X::Fn as X`). Apply across WorkspaceDelta, VineSubscribeCommand, CommandProvider, IPCProvider, GetTreeChildren, and ParseWorkspaceFile.\n\nConsolidate the `SendNotification` call in CocoonManagement.rs to standard multi-line formatting. All IPC and cache usage now resolves exclusively to the canonical Vine library and Cache crate, removing the last traces of local wrapper indirection.\n\nThis completes the absolute-path migration, ensuring Mountain's entire dependency surface delegates to the shared protocol layer with zero local re-exports.",
			"SHA": "3f7f567d44b9af943d4fcbb96a8295379e510f4b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T14:23:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1733,
				39
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Flatten Vine client and cache module indirection\n\nRemove the 12+ local wrapper modules in `Source/Vine/Client` and `Source/Cache` that re-exported canonical implementations. Replace all `crate::Vine::Client::X` and `crate::Cache::Y` calls with absolute paths `::Vine::Client::X` and `::Cache::Y`. This collapses Mountain's gRPC and caching surface to direct delegations, enforcing the Vine library crate as the single source of truth for IPC and cache contracts.\n\nDeleted wrapper modules: `AirServiceProvider`, `AssetMemoryMap::LoadOrInsert`, `PathCanon::Canonicalize`, and all `Vine::Client` atom modules (`MarkShutdown`, `SendRequest`, `SendNotification`, `ConnectToSideCar`, etc.). Kept only dead stubs in `Vine::Client` for compilation compatibility.\n\nThis finalizes the multi-commit migration to absolute-path delegation, reducing code duplication and ensuring all Cocoon↔Mountain IPC flows reference the canonical Vine definitions.",
			"SHA": "6b68fc4cb62aaa2dafecbd25b37b40b72142f87a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T14:13:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1733,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Inline pure-relay notification atoms as RelayToSky one-liners\n\nReplace the remaining deviational notification handlers in MountainVinegRPCService.rs with direct delegations to `::Vine::Server::Notification::Support::RelayToSky::Fn`. The extension lifecycle (ExtensionHostMessage, ExtensionActivated/Deactivated), webview lifecycle (WebviewReady), language settings (setDocumentLanguage), workspace edits (applyEdit), window commands (showTextDocument), tree refresh, progress lifecycle (start/update/complete), output channel operations (create/append/clear/show/dispose/replace), and other Sky-bound notifications are now single-line relay arms with `sky://` routing addresses.\n\nAdd `dev_log!` instrumentation at the dispatch site for ExtensionDeactivated, WebviewReady, and tree.refresh to aid debugging. Remove the now-redundant batch 11–16 comments as the pattern is uniform across all relay atoms.\n\nThis collapses Mountain's notification surface to a pure routing table, enforcing Vine as the single source of truth for all Cocoon→Sky IPC paths while preserving specialized handlers (SetStatusBarText, DisposeStatusBarItem, WebviewPostMessage, etc.) that require coalescing, payload transformation, or Mountain-specific state.",
			"SHA": "2fda74861782e2364f8ace286ff31e8fc8308c96"
		}
	],
